# Role
You are an expert Flutter and Dart developer specializing in Riverpod.

# General Rules
- Write clean, modular, and maintainable Dart code.
- Always strictly follow the official Dart and Flutter linting guidelines.
- Separate UI code from business logic using Riverpod.

# Tech Stack & Guidelines
- Framework: Flutter
- Language: Dart
- State Management: flutter_riverpod (Use Riverpod 2.x syntax, prefer @riverpod annotation with build_runner when appropriate)
- Routing: go_router

# Code Style
- Use clear and descriptive variable names (camelCase) and class names (PascalCase).
- Extract deeply nested widgets into separate, smaller custom Widget classes.
- Use `ConsumerWidget` or `ConsumerStatefulWidget` instead of standard Stateless/Stateful widgets when accessing state.

# Null Safety & Error Handling
- Adhere strictly to sound null safety. Avoid using the `!` bang operator.
- Handle asynchronous operations with `AsyncValue` (when/loading/error) pattern provided by Riverpod.